# Identity-bearing files whose SHA-256 is taken over RAW BYTES. A CRLF checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) silently changes those bytes and therefore the
# hash, which breaks the capture/observation identity gates: the mod's
# _WP2_CAPTURE_SCHEMA_HASH stops matching the schema file, validate_telemetry
# rejects every capture, and the encoder's golden digest moves. Pin them to LF so
# the hash is a property of the content, not of who checked the repo out.
#
# Discovered 2026-07-25 while bumping the capture schema for v127: a worktree
# checkout produced CRLF and yielded a different schema hash than the main
# checkout for byte-identical content.
configs/** text eol=lf
datasets/**/manifest.json text eol=lf
